# core.autocrlf is on for this repo, which would rewrite LF bytes inside binary
# files on checkout. PDFs carry byte offsets in their xref table, so a single
# converted newline makes the file unreadable — mark them binary explicitly.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Deliberately narrow. A repo-wide `* text=auto` would renormalize every file in
# the tree at once, and a concurrent session is committing to this branch.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on this machine checks files out with CRLF. For a shell
# script that means the shebang becomes `#!/bin/sh\r`, which POSIX shells reject
# with "bad interpreter". The hooks are the only shell scripts here, and they are
# the files most likely to be run on a machine that is not this one.
.claude/hooks/* text eol=lf
